@startuml seq-version-edit
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 210
skinparam wrapWidth 190
skinparam shadowing false
title Editing a chapter creates a version\n(spec: node-edit-session.spec.ts · chat-editing.spec.ts · idb-chat-api.service.spec.ts)
' Aliases match docs/specs/component-map.puml.

actor User
participant "CMP_NODE\nChatNodeComponent" as NODE
participant "SVC_EDIT\nNodeEditSession" as EDIT
participant "SVC_CHAT\nChatService (facade)" as SVC
participant "SVC_TREE\nchat-tree-writer" as W
participant "PORT\nChatApiPort" as API
participant "CMP_VERSIONS\nTextVersionPanel /\nNodeVersionDiff" as VER

== 1. Start editing ==
User -> NODE : clicks into a chapter
NODE -> EDIT : begin(chatId, nodeId)
note right of EDIT
  single-session invariant: at most ONE session at a time.
  begin() for the same chat+node reuses it; a different node
  replaces it — but only after the dirty-check (step 3).
end note
NODE -> EDIT : patch(drafts) on every keystroke
EDIT -> EDIT : dirty = draft ≠ baseline\n(text OR attachments, order counts)
note right of EDIT
  node-edit-session.spec: "becomes dirty when draft text diverges",
  "is clean again when drafts are patched back to the baseline".
end note

== 2. Commit the edit ==
User -> NODE : clicks Done / Ctrl+S
NODE -> SVC : editAssistant(chatId, nodeId, content, attachments, thinking, usage?)
SVC -> W : editAssistant(...)
W -> API : editAssistant()
API --> W : saved node
alt backend versioned the row (saved.id ≠ nodeId)
  W -> W : old node isCurrent = false (retired, NOT deleted)
  W -> W : adoptSubtree(oldId → saved.id)\nchildren + activeChildMap re-keyed
  note right of W
    chat-editing.spec: "editAssistant / editUser create a new version
    and reparent children" (idb spec). The previous text stays
    readable — nothing is lost.
  end note
end
W -> W : setActiveChild(saved.parentId, saved.id)\nensureDraftAtLeaf(chatId)
SVC --> NODE : saved
NODE -> EDIT : commit(nodeId)  → session cleared
note right of EDIT
  commit() only clears when THAT node owns the session
  (a late save must not clear someone else's edit).
end note

== 3. Navigating away while dirty ==
User -> NODE : clicks another section
NODE -> EDIT : canLeave?  (or begin() for the other node)
EDIT -> EDIT : dirty ⇒ open confirm dialog\n(reuses SVC_DIALOGS confirm)
alt user confirms discard
  EDIT -> EDIT : abandon(oldNodeId) → switch / leave
else user cancels
  EDIT -> EDIT : keep the old session and the drafts
end
note right of EDIT
  node-edit-session.spec covers: same node reopened in another chat,
  automatic callers never prompted, and "canLeaveChat" on a dirty
  session switching chats.
end note

== 4. Inspecting what changed ==
User -> VER : opens the version panel on the chapter
VER -> SVC : getPriorVersions(nodeId)
SVC --> VER : retired versions (isCurrent = false)
VER -> VER : side-by-side diff (NodeVersionDiff)
note right of VER
  text-version-panel.spec / node-version-diff-dialog.spec assert the
  listing and the diff rendering; the version ROWS themselves are the
  server's/src/app/api's job (idb + routes specs).
end note

@enduml
